# RecallAI — Architectural & Technical Setup Document

## 1. Executive Summary

**RecallAI** is a privacy-first, graph-augmented academic study companion and AI tutor designed to solve the critical flaw of modern conversational tutors: **session amnesia and cognitive isolation**. 

Unlike standard LLM interfaces that treat each chat in a silo, RecallAI introduces a **Graph-backed Long-Term Memory (GraphRAG)** architecture using **FalkorDB** paired with local open-weights inference (**Ollama running Qwen 2.5**). It dynamically extracts student learning signals (recurring mistakes, study goals, conceptual weak spots, and personal identity) and builds an evolving academic knowledge graph. 

When a student queries the system across any conversation or session, RecallAI executes multi-hop graph traversals across academic ontologies (e.g., resolving $F_{net}$ and friction onto inclined planes) to inject mathematically grounded, contextually anchored memories into Qwen's prompt pipeline in real time.

